
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ZFC4Lean in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "ZFC4Lean: A Verified Axiomatic Foundation for Set Theory in Lean 4"
abstract: >-
  ZFC4Lean formalizes Zermelo-Fraenkel set theory with Choice (ZFC) as an
  explicit first-order axiomatic system in Lean 4. The project provides a
  Hilbert-style proof system, model-theoretic semantics with a machine-verified
  soundness theorem, all 10 ZFC axioms as explicit first-order sentences, and
  a formalization of the Continuum Hypothesis. The long-term goal is the first
  Lean 4 machine-verified proof of CH independence.
authors:
  - name: "ZFC4Lean Contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ZFC4Lean/ZFC4Lean"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-13"
keywords:
  - lean4
  - set-theory
  - ZFC
  - formal-verification
  - continuum-hypothesis
  - forcing
  - constructible-universe
  - interactive-theorem-proving
  - mathematical-logic
